{
	"ID": "20260804185002-secvr03",
	"Spec": "2",
	"Type": "NodeDocument",
	"Properties": {
		"id": "20260804185002-secvr03",
		"title": "Secrets and Variables",
		"type": "doc",
		"updated": "20260812170000"
	},
	"Children": [
		{"ID": "20260804224101-secen01", "Type": "NodeHeading", "HeadingLevel": 2, "Properties": {"id": "20260804224101-secen01", "updated": "20260804230000"}, "Children": [{"Type": "NodeText", "Data": "Overview"}]},
		{"ID": "20260804224102-secen02", "Type": "NodeParagraph", "Properties": {"id": "20260804224102-secen02", "updated": "20260804230000"}, "Children": [{"Type": "NodeText", "Data": "Secrets and variables centrally manage reusable values for skills, MCP services, agent tools, and plugins. Secrets are intended for sensitive data such as passwords and API tokens. Their values are encrypted at rest and do not enter AI conversations. Variables are intended for addresses, names, and other non-sensitive parameters. Their values are stored in plain text and may enter AI conversations."}]},
		{"ID": "20260804224103-secen03", "Type": "NodeHeading", "HeadingLevel": 2, "Properties": {"id": "20260804224103-secen03", "updated": "20260804230000"}, "Children": [{"Type": "NodeText", "Data": "Configuration"}]},
		{"ID": "20260804224104-secen04", "Type": "NodeParagraph", "Properties": {"id": "20260804224104-secen04", "updated": "20260804230000"}, "Children": [{"Type": "NodeText", "Data": "Add, edit, or delete secrets and variables in "}, {"Type": "NodeTextMark", "TextMarkType": "kbd", "TextMarkTextContent": "Settings"}, {"Type": "NodeText", "Data": " - "}, {"Type": "NodeTextMark", "TextMarkType": "kbd", "TextMarkTextContent": "Secrets and Variables"}, {"Type": "NodeText", "Data": ". Each item has a name and a value. For compatibility with every reference form, use ASCII letters, digits, and underscores in names, and do not start a name with a digit."}]},
		{"ID": "20260804224105-secen05", "Type": "NodeHeading", "HeadingLevel": 2, "Properties": {"id": "20260804224105-secen05", "updated": "20260804230000"}, "Children": [{"Type": "NodeText", "Data": "Reference forms"}]},
		{"ID": "20260804224106-secen06", "Type": "NodeParagraph", "Properties": {"id": "20260804224106-secen06", "updated": "20260804230000"}, "Children": [{"Type": "NodeText", "Data": "Use the shorthand "}, {"Type": "NodeTextMark", "TextMarkType": "code", "TextMarkTextContent": "$NAME"}, {"Type": "NodeText", "Data": " or "}, {"Type": "NodeTextMark", "TextMarkType": "code", "TextMarkTextContent": "${NAME}"}, {"Type": "NodeText", "Data": ", or use the namespaced forms "}, {"Type": "NodeTextMark", "TextMarkType": "code", "TextMarkTextContent": "{{secrets.NAME}}"}, {"Type": "NodeText", "Data": " and "}, {"Type": "NodeTextMark", "TextMarkType": "code", "TextMarkTextContent": "{{vars.NAME}}"}, {"Type": "NodeText", "Data": ". Namespaced forms are unambiguous and are recommended in shared configurations and skills."}]},
		{"ID": "20260804224107-secen07", "Type": "NodeParagraph", "Properties": {"id": "20260804224107-secen07", "updated": "20260804230000"}, "Children": [{"Type": "NodeText", "Data": "If a secret and variable have the same name, shorthand references resolve to the secret first where both stores are supported. Namespaced references select the intended store explicitly. If a name is not found, the placeholder remains unchanged so missing configuration is visible."}]},
		{"ID": "20260804224108-secen08", "Type": "NodeHeading", "HeadingLevel": 2, "Properties": {"id": "20260804224108-secen08", "updated": "20260812170000"}, "Children": [{"Type": "NodeText", "Data": "Examples"}]},
		{"ID": "20260804224109-secen09", "Type": "NodeParagraph", "Properties": {"id": "20260804224109-secen09", "updated": "20260812170000"}, "Children": [{"Type": "NodeText", "Data": "For example, after adding a secret named "}, {"Type": "NodeTextMark", "TextMarkType": "code", "TextMarkTextContent": "API_TOKEN"}, {"Type": "NodeText", "Data": " and a variable named "}, {"Type": "NodeTextMark", "TextMarkType": "code", "TextMarkTextContent": "WORKSPACE"}, {"Type": "NodeText", "Data": ", reference them in the HTTP headers or stdio environment variables of an agent MCP service as follows:"}]},
		{"ID": "20260804224110-secen10", "Type": "NodeCodeBlock", "IsFencedCodeBlock": true, "CodeBlockFenceChar": 96, "CodeBlockFenceLen": 3, "CodeBlockOpenFence": "YGBg", "CodeBlockInfo": "anNvbg==", "CodeBlockCloseFence": "YGBg", "Properties": {"id": "20260804224110-secen10", "updated": "20260804230000"}, "Children": [{"Type": "NodeCodeBlockFenceOpenMarker", "Data": "```", "CodeBlockFenceLen": 3}, {"Type": "NodeCodeBlockFenceInfoMarker", "CodeBlockInfo": "anNvbg=="}, {"Type": "NodeCodeBlockCode", "Data": "{\n  \"Authorization\": \"Bearer {{secrets.API_TOKEN}}\",\n  \"X-Workspace\": \"{{vars.WORKSPACE}}\"\n}\n"}, {"Type": "NodeCodeBlockFenceCloseMarker", "Data": "```", "CodeBlockFenceLen": 3}]},
		{"ID": "20260804224111-secen11", "Type": "NodeParagraph", "Properties": {"id": "20260804224111-secen11", "updated": "20260812170000"}, "Children": [{"Type": "NodeText", "Data": "A stdio MCP service inherits only the kernel environment variables selected by the user, and its environment variable entries can use the references above. Referencing a secret provides its plaintext value to the program and its child processes. The agent's built-in HTTP request tool also resolves secrets and variables in URLs, HTTP headers, and request bodies. For example, a URL can be written as "}, {"Type": "NodeTextMark", "TextMarkType": "code", "TextMarkTextContent": "{{vars.API_BASE}}/v1/items"}, {"Type": "NodeText", "Data": ". Skill bodies and chat messages can use variables. Secret placeholders are not expanded in AI conversations; they are resolved only when a supported tool or MCP configuration sends the request."}]},
		{"ID": "20260804224112-secen12", "Type": "NodeParagraph", "Properties": {"id": "20260804224112-secen12", "updated": "20260804230000"}, "Children": [{"Type": "NodeText", "Data": "Plugins can also read or resolve secrets and variables through APIs. Verify a plugin's source and permissions before installation because a plugin with secret access can obtain plaintext values at runtime."}]},
		{"ID": "20260804224113-secen13", "Type": "NodeHeading", "HeadingLevel": 2, "Properties": {"id": "20260804224113-secen13", "updated": "20260804230000"}, "Children": [{"Type": "NodeText", "Data": "Security recommendations"}]},
		{"ID": "20260804224114-secen14", "Type": "NodeParagraph", "Properties": {"id": "20260804224114-secen14", "updated": "20260804230000"}, "Children": [{"Type": "NodeText", "Data": "Do not store passwords, access tokens, or private keys as variables, and do not write sensitive values directly in chat messages, skill bodies, or ordinary configuration. After deleting or replacing a secret, review the skills, MCP services, and plugin configurations that use it. For how the agent uses these settings, see "}, {"Type": "NodeTextMark", "TextMarkType": "block-ref", "TextMarkBlockRefID": "20260804171004-aiagt03", "TextMarkBlockRefSubtype": "s", "TextMarkTextContent": "AI Agent"}, {"Type": "NodeText", "Data": "."}]}
	]
}
